    "notes": "NVIDIA DGX Spark (ASUS Ascent GX10, GB10) on Ubuntu 24.04 / DGX OS, driver 580.173.02, CUDA 13.0. SparkInfer stack at commit 960652b of https://github.com/0xBakeer/DeepSeek-v4-Flash-One-DGX-Spark (branch atlas-run-20260824), a fork of MiaAI-Lab/DeepSeek-v4-Flash-One-DGX-Spark; compose.yml pins the image ghcr.io/0xsero/deepseek-v4-flash-0731-spark-sparkinfer@sha256:2e077489a83a0360952828051fe7f7a32c1801e5ce8436d85f7267583d614ff4 by digest and bind-mounts twelve patch files over it, so image plus commit together define the stack. Model revision 22f28d32b9b29b4352eaa380ff8c2c170b2847ab. This run used the upstream 384k single-sequence profile with the refusal ablation on, carried explicitly in args: max-model-len 384000, max-num-seqs 1, gpu-memory-utilization 0.94, ablate true (upstream false). Thinking was OFF for this workload via chat_template_kwargs {\"thinking\": false}, because with thinking on the 3,000-token output budget is consumed by the thought block and every item comes back empty. The machine is otherwise idle."
